rted-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Keep the question word, but **remove inversion** in the report.","Keep when, then use **they would compare** in statement order.","Choose **they would compare the survey results**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The verb after would stays base.","B":"Keep when, then use **they would compare** in statement order.","C":"The subject must precede would inside the embedded question.","D":"Would takes a bare infinitive."}}},{"id":"006e73f2-d549-5937-aca9-c34a2fa8a931","topicSlug":"reported-questions","level":"B1","prompt":"Report the instruction: “Please compare the survey results.” → She asked us ____.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"to compare the survey results"},{"id":"B","text":"compare the survey results"},{"id":"C","text":"compared the survey results"},{"id":"D","text":"that compare the survey results"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Report the instruction with **ask + person + to-infinitive**.","explanation":"A reported request uses **asked us to compare**.","keywords":["reported-command"],"skill":"reported-command","contextKey":"reported-questions-48","fingerprint":"e239ea4fd656cf5e6e72ae5e97e0b835044da18f9ef1109b0d9be1a8a65465c8","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Report the instruction with **ask + person + to-infinitive**.","A reported request uses **asked us to compare**.","Choose **to compare the survey results**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"A reported request uses **asked us to compare**.","B":"The reported-request pattern needs to before the infinitive.","C":"A past form does not complete asked us in this request pattern.","D":"That would need a complete finite clause, not a bare verb."}}},{"id":"a936155b-5483-5f6d-a870-3461c79c3a7d","topicSlug":"reported-questions","level":"B1","prompt":"Report “Do not compare the survey results yet.” → She told us ____.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"do not compare the survey results yet"},{"id":"B","text":"not compare the survey results yet"},{"id":"C","text":"not to compared the survey results yet"},{"id":"D","text":"not to compare the survey results yet"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Put **not before to** in a reported negative instruction.","explanation":"The negative reported instruction is **told us not to compare**.","keywords":["negative-reported-command"],"skill":"negative-reported-command","contextKey":"reported-questions-48","fingerprint":"b5a3b58dc6e8831c3d9df82b800b8544ff09f2a466070e85369171e87a85aa7e","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Put **not before to** in a reported negative instruction.","The negative reported instruction is **told us not to compare**.","Choose **not to compare the survey results yet**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This keeps the direct imperative instead of using a reported infinitive.","B":"To is missing before the infinitive.","C":"After to, use the base form, not the past form.","D":"The negative reported instruction is **told us not to compare**."}}},{"id":"9c166cda-769d-5ed6-aeda-ba7746e3bc98","topicSlug":"reported-questions","level":"B1","prompt":"Report the question with statement order: “Did she prepare the evening meal?” → He asked whether ____.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"did she prepare the evening meal"},{"id":"B","text":"she did prepared the evening meal"},{"id":"C","text":"she had prepared the evening meal"},{"id":"D","text":"had she prepared the evening meal"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"An embedded question uses **subject before verb**.","explanation":"After **whether**, use subject **she** before **had prepared** in this backshifted report.","keywords":["reported-yes-no"],"skill":"reported-yes-no","contextKey":"reported-questions-49","fingerprint":"271e061b65e4779b2a4d4254e66a6eeb61253498d250514a3a431527fea9d514","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["An embedded question uses **subject before verb**.","After **whether**, use subject **she** before **had prepared** in this backshifted report.","Choose **she had prepared the evening meal**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This keeps direct-question do-support and inversion.","B":"After did, a main verb must be base; this is not the requested backshifted structure.","C":"After **whether**, use subject **she** before **had prepared** in this backshifted report.","D":"This keeps question inversion inside the embedded clause."}}},{"id":"27d90657-1584-555e-a436-a76a82c6eade","topicSlug":"reported-questions","level":"B1","prompt":"Report with backshift: “When will they prepare the evening meal?” → She asked when ____.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"they would prepared the evening meal"},{"id":"B","text":"they would prepare the evening meal"},{"id":"C","text":"would they prepare the evening meal"},{"id":"D","text":"they would to prepare the evening meal"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Keep the question word, but **remove inversion** in the report.","explanation":"Keep when, then use **they would prepare** in statement order.","keywords":["reported-wh-order"],"skill":"reported-wh-order","contextKey":"reported-questions-49","fingerprint":"f089bed262a3b748c75c095b82e65dd0e1d63622950af23c9875d22bfcd7ab84","source":