in this request pattern.","C":"That would need a complete finite clause, not a bare verb.","D":"A reported request uses **asked us to prepare**."}}},{"id":"2131d0b4-6f93-5c88-a7df-424ade537c41","topicSlug":"reported-questions","level":"B1","prompt":"Report “Do not prepare the evening meal yet.” → She told us ____.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"not to prepared the evening meal yet"},{"id":"B","text":"not to prepare the evening meal yet"},{"id":"C","text":"do not prepare the evening meal yet"},{"id":"D","text":"not prepare the evening meal yet"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Put **not before to** in a reported negative instruction.","explanation":"The negative reported instruction is **told us not to prepare**.","keywords":["negative-reported-command"],"skill":"negative-reported-command","contextKey":"reported-questions-49","fingerprint":"e4d1d5beed3b481822763286a653e35356b23e8abe884788e2bba4d9aae2028c","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Put **not before to** in a reported negative instruction.","The negative reported instruction is **told us not to prepare**.","Choose **not to prepare the evening meal yet**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"After to, use the base form, not the past form.","B":"The negative reported instruction is **told us not to prepare**.","C":"This keeps the direct imperative instead of using a reported infinitive.","D":"To is missing before the infinitive."}}},{"id":"77635238-5608-559f-a748-fbcf0474031a","topicSlug":"reported-questions","level":"B1","prompt":"Report the question with statement order: “Did she repair the rowing boat?” → He asked whether ____.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"she did repaired the rowing boat"},{"id":"B","text":"she had repaired the rowing boat"},{"id":"C","text":"had she repaired the rowing boat"},{"id":"D","text":"did she repair the rowing boat"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"An embedded question uses **subject before verb**.","explanation":"After **whether**, use subject **she** before **had repaired** in this backshifted report.","keywords":["reported-yes-no"],"skill":"reported-yes-no","contextKey":"reported-questions-50","fingerprint":"fb787f1018cccaefe30573a7daaa5ab0944e3e7685cd2d91ea896f9d099c3632","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["An embedded question uses **subject before verb**.","After **whether**, use subject **she** before **had repaired** in this backshifted report.","Choose **she had repaired the rowing boat**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"After did, a main verb must be base; this is not the requested backshifted structure.","B":"After **whether**, use subject **she** before **had repaired** in this backshifted report.","C":"This keeps question inversion inside the embedded clause.","D":"This keeps direct-question do-support and inversion."}}},{"id":"db55f881-a145-5a1f-a635-7815732d060c","topicSlug":"reported-questions","level":"B1","prompt":"Report with backshift: “When will they repair the rowing boat?” → She asked when ____.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"they would repaired the rowing boat"},{"id":"B","text":"they would repair the rowing boat"},{"id":"C","text":"would they repair the rowing boat"},{"id":"D","text":"they would to repair the rowing boat"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Keep the question word, but **remove inversion** in the report.","explanation":"Keep when, then use **they would repair** in statement order.","keywords":["reported-wh-order"],"skill":"reported-wh-order","contextKey":"reported-questions-50","fingerprint":"e431743f2c2dd43125a212b1c8cac0e754863a7bb69a09cbdcfbdcdb17da56c2","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Keep the question word, but **remove inversion** in the report.","Keep when, then use **they would repair** in statement order.","Choose **they would repair the rowing boat**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The verb after would stays base.","B":"Keep when, then use **they would repair** in statement order.","C":"The subject must precede would inside the embedded question.","D":"Would takes a bare infinitive."}}},{"id":"758393ff-7566-58d3-adc7-162c7c86f4c0","topicSlug":"reported-questions","level":"B1","prompt":"Report the instruction: “Please repair the rowing boat.” → She asked us ____.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"that repair the rowing boat"},{"id":"B","text":"to repair the rowing boat"},{"id":"C","text":"repair the rowing boat"},{"id":"D","text":"repaired the rowing boat"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Report the instruction with **ask + person + to-infinitive**.","explanation":"A reported request uses **asked us to repair**.","keywords":["reported-command"],"skill":"reported-command","contextKey":"reported-questions-50","fingerprint":"efa9b16555e5669b240891cc6ba6a02ba2e05b6af4e170341feee31ffd4854ec","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Report the instruction with **ask + person + to-infinitive**.","A reported request uses **asked us to repair**.","Choose **to repair the rowing boat**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"That would need a complete finite clause, not a bare verb.","B":"A reported request uses **asked us to repair**.","C":"The reported-request pattern needs to before the infinitive.","D":"A past form does not complete asked us in this request pattern."}}},{"id":"11aed94e-94ed-5797-a8b1-2a655b4eff50","topicSlug":"reported-questions","level":"B1","prompt":"Report “Do not repair the rowing boat yet.” → She told us ____.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"not to repair the rowing boat yet"},{"id":"B","text":"do not repair the rowing boat yet"},{"id":"C","text":"not repair the rowing boat yet"},{"id":"D","text":"not to repaired the rowing boat yet"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Put **not before to** in a reported negative instruction.","explanation":"The negative reported instruction is **told us not to repair**.","keywords":["negative-reported-command"],"skill":"negative-reported-command","contextKey":"reported-questions-50","fingerprint":"8f0e752a066fcb10ecf3b151c9a310ed7c5c7f631f21f717812ae4b462b4cbc6","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Put **not before to** in a reported negative instruction.","The negative reported instruction is **told us not to repair**.","Choose **not to repair the rowing boat yet**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The negative reported instruction is **told us not to repair**.","B":"This keeps the direct imperative instead of using a reported infinitive.","C":"To is missing before the infinitive.","D":"After to, use the base form, not the past form."}}}],"chapter":{"introduction":["Embed a question in a report without carrying direct-question word order into the embedded clause.","The form tells you how to build the sentence; the context tells you why that form is useful. Read each section with both questions in mind. The examples make one contrast at a time, while the practice mixes the skills so that you learn to recognise the pattern yourself."],"rules":[{"title":"Yes/no questions use if or whether","explanation":"A reported yes/no question commonly starts with asked if or asked whether. The embedded clause has **statement order**, with subject before verb. A report of a question is not itself necessarily a question and usually ends with a full stop.","pattern":"She asked **whether I was ready**.","commonMistakes":["She asked was I ready keeps direct-question order where an embedded clause is needed."],"examples":["Report the question with statement order: “Did she prepare the visitor guide?” → He asked whether **she had prepared the visitor guide**.","Report the question with statement order: “Did she restore the old portrait?” → He asked whether **she had restored the old portrait**."],"skill":"form"},{"title":"Wh-questions keep the question word","explanation":"Who, what, where, when, why and how stay at the start of the embedded clause. Remove do-support when it only formed the direct question and put the lexical verb into the appropriate tense.","pattern":"“Where do you work?” → She asked **where I worked**.","commonMistakes":["Where did I work inside a statement report incorrectly retains inversion and do-support."],"examples":["Report with backshift: “When will they prepare the visitor guide?” → She asked when **they would prepare the visitor guide**.","Report with backshift: “When will they restore the old portrait?” → She asked when **they would restore the old portrait**."],"skill":"meaning"},{"title":"Commands use an infinitive pattern","explanation":"Tell or ask someone **to do** something can report an instruction or request. A negative command uses **not to do**. Keep the person receiving the instruction as the object of told or asked.","pattern":"She told us **to wait**. / She asked us **not to leave**.","commonMistakes":["Told us wait omits to in this reported-command pattern."],"examples":["Report the instruction: “Please prepare the visitor guide.” → She asked us **to prepare the visitor guide**.","Report the instruction: “Please restore the old portrait.” → She asked us **to restore the old portrait**."],"skill":"contrast"},{"title":"Adjust viewpoint carefully","explanation":"Pronouns, time words and backshift depend on the reporting context, just as in reported statements. Subject questions require special care: Who called? already has subject-first order and does not contain removable do-support.","pattern":"He asked **who had called**.","commonMistakes":["Whether is preferred or required in some structures, such as whether to leave and after prepositions; if cannot replace it everywhere."],"examples":["Report “Do not prepare the visitor guide yet.” → She told us **not to prepare the visitor guide yet**.","Report “Do not restore the old portrait yet.” → She told us **not to restore the old portrait yet**."],"skill":"application"}],"recap":["She asked **whether I was ready**.","“Where do you work?” → She asked **where I worked**.","She told us **to wait**. / She asked us **not to leave**.","He asked **who had called**."]},"stage":"5 · Complex sentences","prerequisites":["reported-statements"]}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT(version,slug) DO NOTHING;
DO $guard$ BEGIN
 IF EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM grammar.grammar_topics WHERE slug='reported-questions' AND source_metadata->>'version' IS DISTINCT FROM 'core-2026-09-v3') THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Topic belongs to another release'; END IF;
 IF EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM grammar.grammar_quiz_items WHERE topic_slug='reported-questions' AND source_metadata->>'version' IS DISTINCT FROM 'core-2026-09-v3') THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Questions belong to another release'; END IF;
END $guard$;
INSERT INTO grammar.grammar_topics(slug,title,level,order_index,summary,guidance,learning_goals,rules,tips,source,source_metadata)
SELECT j->>'slug',j->>'title',j->>'level',(j->>'order')::integer,j->>'summary',j->>'guidance',ARRAY(SELECT jsonb_array_elements_text(j->'learningGoals')),j->'rules',ARRAY(SELECT jsonb_array_elements_text(j->'tips')),'seed','{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-questions"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending","contentHash":"e49c6c64b6333354230b05b223ded19e0e7519c1828bf3f36aee778f9f3f39c4","sources":[{"id":"bc-reported-questions","title":"Reported speech: questions","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar/b1-b2/reported-speech-questions","publisher":"British Council LearnEnglish","use":"Grammar guidance and scope only. Original explanations and practice; no publisher exercise reproduced.","reviewedOn":"2026-09-13"}]}'::jsonb FROM (SELECT payload j FROM grammar.content_catalog_topics WHERE version='core-2026-09-v3' AND slug='reported-questions') p
ON CONFLICT(slug) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO grammar.grammar_quiz_items(id,topic_slug,level,prompt,choices,answer_id,hint,explanation,keywords,source,fingerprint,source_metadata)
SELECT (q->>'id')::uuid,q->>'topicSlug',q->>'level',q->>'prompt',q->'choices',q->>'answerId',q->>'hint',q->>'explanation',ARRAY(SELECT jsonb_array_elements_text(q->'keywords')),'seed',q->>'fingerprint',(q->'provenance')||jsonb_build_object('contentHash','e49c6c64b6333354230b05b223ded19e0e7519c1828bf3f36aee778f9f3f39c4','skill',q->>'skill','contextKey',q->>'contextKey','teaching',q->'teaching')
FROM grammar.content_catalog_topics t CROSS JOIN LATERAL jsonb_array_elements(t.payload->'quizItems') q WHERE t.version='core-2026-09-v3' AND t.slug='reported-questions'
ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
DO $verify$ BEGIN
 IF NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM grammar.content_catalog_topics WHERE version='core-2026-09-v3' AND slug='reported-questions' AND payload_md5='123d18130398bcd0c34d9a7e2fc9e189') THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Full payload mismatch'; END IF;
 IF (SELECT count(*) FROM grammar.grammar_quiz_items WHERE topic_slug='reported-questions')<>200 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Question count mismatch'; END IF;
END $verify$;
COMMIT;
